00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,740
Oh, excuse me.

260
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:43,380
I forgot who I was talking to.

261
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:46,660
It is replete with stinkiosity.

262
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,020
But at least you can spell.

263
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,460
The others, they can't even spell.

264
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,900
You spell words that nobody knows.

265
00:14:57,160 --> 00:15:01,560
Mucilis. What in the hell is mucilis?

266
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:04,240
Well, it's, um...

267
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,440
It's basically... a slimy glop.

268
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,380
Then you call it slimy glop.

269
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:13,820
People know what slimy glop is.

270
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,640
Yeah, well, I just felt like I was going to die.

271
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:19,500
Felt is for pool tables.

272
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,840
You start Monday.

273
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,980
Thank you, but I don't think I want the job.

274
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,140
Around the fourth turn, it's Nice Girl in the lead.

275
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:32,280
Come on, Undulate!

276
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:36,920
It's still Nice Girl a full six lengths ahead of Hedge Trimmer with Undulate a

277
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:41,140
distant third. Hey, guys, it looks like Undulate's gonna be very late.

278
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:44,340
Relax. Nice Girl always starts strong.

279
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:47,060
She'll fade. And Nice Girl's starting to fade.

280
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,060
Now, come on.

281
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:48,960
You can do it, Undulate.

282
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:52,900
Don't worry. She'll make her move on the outside, right here.

283
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:53,720
And let's see.

284
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:56,060
Moving on the outside, it's Undulate.

285
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:57,400
Look at her go.

286
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:59,340
And they're moving down the final stretch.

287
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,300
They're neck and neck.

288
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,140
It's Nice Girl, Undulate.

289
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,900
Nice Girl, Undulate.

290
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:06,340
And at the finish, it's...

291
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:09,040
Undulate! By a nose hair!

292
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,720
And she'll pay off at nine to one, folks.

293
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:13,720
Nine to one.

294
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,520
Holy cow, that's $450.

295
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,940
What? I -I think Jerry called from O.T.B.

296
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,000
What do we do fast, Benny?

297
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:23,260
We keep the $450, let it ride on Nail -Biter in the night.

298
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:25,740
Guys, I think you should quit while you're ahead.

299
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:30,160
Jason! Maggie, that's $450.

300
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,640
You put that in a rollover account with interest to wait.

301
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:33,500
Aw, come on.

302
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:36,140
We could teach him this gambling lesson another time.

303
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:42,200
It's okay. Boys, I say this is no time to stop.

304
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,000
You know you got it.

305
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,980
You got that touch.

306
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:45,640
All right, Jerry.

307
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:47,100
Put it all on Nail Biter to win.

308
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,220
Oh, hi, Carol.

309
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:53,840
How did it go with Simmons?

310
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,340
Fine, thank you.

311
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:56,040
I got the job.

312
00:16:56,540 --> 00:17:01,000
Oh, really? Well, congratulations, honey.

313
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,140
That's wonderful. Carol got the job on the paper.

314
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,940
Yeah! Arthur, Arthur.

315
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,420
I turned it down.

316
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:24,780
Can I come in?

317
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:30,620
Sure. What are you doing?

318
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,000
Cleaning the garbage out of my way.

319
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:38,960
Carol, how come you turned the job down?

320
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,780
I mean, it really seemed like you had your heart set on it.

321
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:45,060
Yeah, well, that was before I realized there's nothing really creative about

322
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:47,700
journalism. I mean, all you do is regurgitate facts.

323
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,620
If I were gonna be a writer, I'd rather do a novel.

324
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,160
At least people don't train their puppies on Moby Dick.

325
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:04,780
Carol, I can understand you being angry at me for my criticism of your article.

326
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,540
Why should I be angry?

327
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,940
Simmons gave me the job.

328
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:18,280
I know. I know, and I guess what I'm trying to say is, well, honey, it's always

329
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,740
tricky giving criticism to someone you love.

330
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,820
And I guess I just didn't do a very good job.

331
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:30,300
Obviously, Simmons was very happy with what you did, and I'm glad that I was wrong.

332
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:36,860
No. Pardon me?

333
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,400
I said no, OK?

334
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,060
Are you happy?

335
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,960
He said everything you said only works.

336
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,200
He said my article was...

337
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:50,900
replete with stinkeosity.

338
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,720
But you said that you got the job.

339
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:57,880
Yeah, well, that was only because all the other articles were repleted with

340
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:03,660
stinkeosity. Aw, honey, I am so sorry.

341
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:06,920
He said he didn't even know what mucus was.

342
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:12,200
Well, that's... that's just his stupidity, sweetheart.

343
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,500
Everybody knows what newcomers is.

344
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:18,780
I'll never be able to write like you.

345
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,740
Oh, oh, hold on, hold on, honey.

346
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,140
That's just not true.

347
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:28,320
Now, maybe you were reaching a little, but you have great natural ability.

348
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,080
You're just saying that.

349
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:39,240
Hey. Didn't I establish myself last night as someone who isn't afraid to tell the

350
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:46,180
truth? Yeah. Even if it does mean crushing a little kid's ego.

351
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:54,740
You really think I might have natural ability?

352
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,400
I dug this out of the attic this afternoon.

353
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:04,860
And I thought that you might like to take a look at it.

354
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,280
The letter I wrote from camp five years ago?

355
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:17,040
Read it. Dear Mom and Dad,

356
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:23,260
camp is fun, except for the rash I got when I tried to find out what poison sumac

357
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:29,100
looks like, except for the kids teasing anyone who's small or fat or left -handed.

358
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:32,080
Except for missing you and baby Ben.

359
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:36,260
And even Michael Little, but don't tell him.

360
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,600
Bring my chemistry set and potato chips on visiting day.

361
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:45,000
Love, Carol. That's not so good.

362
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:51,160
Hey, didn't we bring your chemistry set and your potato chips?

363
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:56,320
Yeah. Then you got your point across.

364
00:20:57,400 --> 00:21:01,600
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah, I see what you're saying.

365
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,520
But I still think it could have been better.

366
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:07,320
Now, what makes you say that?

367
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:11,300
Well, as I remember, you brought Mike, too.

368
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:17,560
Mmm. And this is unbelievable.

369
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:22,480
Coming around the final turn, it's Nailbiter by 18 lengths, running a distance

370
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:26,040
second as Slim's Frog, with Arnold's Dream Date in third position.

371
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,400
Whoo! Nailbiter! And it's Nailbiter by 20 lengths.

372
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,900
Nailbiter, woo! And Nailbiter's at the final pole.

373
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:35,480
And he must be a full 25 lengths ahead.

374
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:37,540
That horse could walk in from here.

375
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:41,000
Go, Nailbiter! I'll never have to work again!

376
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,820
Uh -oh. Ladies and gentlemen, wait a minute.

377
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:45,180
There's been an accident.

378
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:47,740
Nailbiter has tripped and gone down.

379
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,820
The horse is on the ground.

380
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:53,320
In all my years at the track, I've never seen anything like this.

381
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,680
Get up! Get up!

382
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:58,200
A foot from the finish line, maybe two feet.

383
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,820
And the jockey is trying to drag the horse across the finish line.

384
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,340
Well, stick him up and carry him.

385
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:04,720
This is amazing.

386
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:08,760
A 94 -pound man trying to drag a racehorse by one leg.

387
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:09,960
He's too strong.

388
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:12,900
Come on, you little munchkin.

389
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:16,540
Look out. Coming up to the outside is Slim's Frog.

390
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:20,160
And the winner is Slim's Frog.

391
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:21,460
No! Oh, no.

392
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:25,740
It was just...

393
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:27,800
I hope you boys have learned your lesson, then.

394
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:35,160
Oh, look at here.

395
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:39,280
X -rays reveal that nail biters suffered a fractured fibula.

396
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:44,780
Oh. Trainer Jim Sheppard immediately announced that his prize thoroughbred would be

397
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,640
put out to stud.

398
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:49,500
What stud? Mom?

399
00:22:51,860 --> 00:22:57,520
Well, Ben, uh, sometimes when a boy horse gets hurt, they use him to get lots and

400
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,920
lots of girl horses pregnant.

401
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:00,860
That's very good.

402
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:06,260
Oh! Oh! Oh, my leg!

403
00:23:07,980 --> 00:23:11,520
Oh! Oh! Oh!

404
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:14,880
Oh! Oh! Oh!
